n" [:option {:value "19016119"} "Kayak Singles, 1,000 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "19016157"} "Kayak Fours, 500 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "19016169"} "Canadian Singles, 1,000 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "19016188"} "Canadian Doubles, 1,000 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "19016207"} "Kayak Singles, 200 metres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "19016226"} "Kayak Singles, 500 metres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "19016245"} "Kayak Doubles, 500 metres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "19016264"} "Kayak Fours, 500 metres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "19016276"} "Canadian Singles, 200 metres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "19016295"} "Canadian Doubles, 500 metres, Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "255007"} "1936"] "\n" [:option {:value "255031"} "1948"] "\n" [:option {:value "255059"} "1952"] "\n" [:option {:value "255095"} "1956"] "\n" [:option {:value "255133"} "1960"] "\n" [:option {:value "255240"} "1964"] "\n" [:option {:value "255302"} "1968"] "\n" [:option {:value "255366"} "1972"] "\n" [:option {:value "255482"} "1976"] "\n" [:option {:value "255620"} "1980"] "\n" [:option {:value "255714"} "1984"] "\n" [:option {:value "255822"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "255967"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "256104"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "256235"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "256346"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "258770"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "307048"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "353482"} "2016"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/163"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Kayak Doubles, 1,000 metres, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "4 –  5 August 2021"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2129"} "Sea Forest Waterway, 6-44, 3chome, Uminomori, Koto-ku, Tokyo Bay, Tokyo, Japan"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/19016138"} "32 from 14 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "This is one of the four events to be held at every Summer Games since canoeing was introduced in 1936, making its 20th appearance in 2021. The reigning world champions, " [:a {:href "/athletes/116560"} "Max Hoff"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/143394"} "Jacob Schopf"] ", and reigning Olympic champions, " [:a {:href "/athletes/134141"} "Max Rendschmidt"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/125322"} "Marcus Gross"] ", were all from Germany, but only Hoff and Schopf competed in Tokyo. Their main rivals were expected to come from Spain’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/125453"} "Francisco Cubelos"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/133654"} "Inigo Pena"] ", the silver medallists at the 2018 and 2019 ICF World Championships."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the preliminaries, the Spaniards won their heat, but the Germans were surprisingly defeated by an unknown pair of 22-year-olds from Australia, " [:a {:href "/athletes/140745"} "Thomas Green"] " and the South African-born " [:a {:href "/athletes/140744"} "Jean van der Westhuyzen"] ". Van der Westhuyzen grew up idolising Hoff, and even had his picture as his screen saver on his mobile phone."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The Australians and Germans both won their heats in the semi-finals, and everybody eagerly anticipated their battle in the A Final, and they were not disappointed. Australia took the lead right from the start and, after a close-fought race with the German pair, Green and van der Westhuyzen finally claimed a surprise gold medal. The Czech pair of " [:a {:href "/athletes/142094"} "Radek Slouf"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/125290"} "Josef Dostal"] " were not only team-mates but were also best friends, and they won the bronze."] "\n\n" [:p {} "It was the first international regatta for Green and van der Westhuyzen as a K-2 combination. Due to the global pandemic situation, and Australia’s tough lockdown laws, the duo trained and prepared only at home for the previous two seasons, not being able to figure on the international canoeing scene. This made their achievement more surprising and remarkable, as they won Australia´s first ever Olympic gold medal in this event."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Pair"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "QF"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "9/6"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/140744"} "Jean van der Westhuyzen"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/140745"} "Tom Green"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUS.png"}] "AUS"]] [:td {} "3:08.773 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "3:17.077 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "3:15.280 (1 h1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "114/120"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/116560"} "Max Hoff"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/143394"} "Jacob Schopf"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} "3:09.830 (2 h1)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "3:17.554 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "3:15.584 (2 h1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "79/82"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/125290"} "Josef Dostál"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/142094"} "Radek Šlouf"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/count